window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["audi/a6-c6"]={"a6-c6-facelift-acc-distance-setting-in-mmi":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A6 C6 4F facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the distance of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) on the menu in Audi MMI 3G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>13 – Distance control</strong></strong> ” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 7</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart MMI (MENU + CAR 10 sec).</em></p>\n<p><em>For the cruise control menu, press CAR then driver assistance then Adaptive cruise control, you can choose “Distance” 4 distance selection modes</em>.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7452-7b2530cd.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7166-a399eb74.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-activate-dvd-playback-while-driving-vim":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to remove the MMI protection and continue watching a DVD or video while driving (Video in Motion).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Step 1: Retrieving the MMI 2G/3G serial number</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>“for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or<strong>“07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Advanced Ident -1A</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Retrieve serial number (if more than one, use the <strong>first</strong> one!)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_mmi_plus_5f_seriennummer-PNG-12291981.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Calculating the security code</strong></p>\n<p>Enter the serial number previously retrieved from the website (your choice, subject to availability):  </p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.audienthusiasts.com/Articles_VIM.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AUDIENTHUSIATS VIM</a></p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.bestcarmods.com/vim/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">BESTCARMODS VIM</a></p>\n<p>The site will display your security code.<br/><em>An alternative security code is also generated.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Enter security code</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>“for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or<strong>“07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Secure access -16</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Enter security code <br/><em>(Use alternative security code if first code does not work)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 4: Removing the protection</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>“for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or<strong>“07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation -10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>48</strong> for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or Channel <strong>63</strong> for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to <strong>255</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 5: Restart the MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press MENU + Wheel + Top right button</p>","a6-c6-facelift-activate-mmi-3g-hidden-menu":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden green menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI 3G. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 6</strong> </em>and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>No need to restart the MMI.</em></p>\n<p><em><em><em><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (simultaneously for 6 seconds), or press the CAR button first.</em></em></em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a7_mmi_plus-bb5ba729.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g-217db9e1.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> select the “Bootloader” option!</p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>","a6-c6-facelift-activation-of-gearshift-recommendation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the gearshift recommendation. The gearshift recommendation is then displayed in the lower section of the ODB. Only available from model year 2009.    <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>“<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“5</strong>“.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/check_aiguille-9b803756.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7102-675f485c.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-bluetooth-mmi-3g-activation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth with an Audi MMI 3G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Activate Bluetooth in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>main &gt; diagnostics &gt; settings &gt; Tel settings misc</p>\n<p>Select [no WLAN / no NAD / BT / HFP] 4 /16</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 3: Bluetooth activation with VCDS</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong> and then click on ” “.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 17</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Module_5F_Adaptation_Channel17-d3fc3a63.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-change-mmi-3g-start-logo":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to modify the Splash Screen of the MMI 3G. <br/><br/><em>For a customized logo see tuto: A6 (C6) Facelift – MMI 3G/3GP customized splash screen logo</em></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong> </p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Change the start logo in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carcodingvehicle -&gt; configuration line</p>\n<p><em>Select the desired display:</em></p>\n<p><em>[<strong>unknown] 1/5</strong> (Standard home screen)</em><br/><em>[<strong>standard] 2/5</strong> (Standard welcome screen)</em><br/><em>[<strong>S-line] 3/5</strong> (Standard welcome screen)</em><br/><em>[<strong>S-model] 4/5</strong> (S welcome screen depending on model)</em><br/><em>[<strong>RS-Model] 5/5</strong> (RS welcome screen)</em></p>\n<p>Then <em>select “Update Splashscreen (according car line)”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6875-a1c0ed3d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6876-ad94c126.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6877-7c285f46.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6878-168e78a3.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-enable-mmi-3g-cd-dvd-extraction":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A6 C6 4F facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates CD/DVD extraction in the DVD player. Allows you to import / copy all CD/DVD / SD card content to the MMI 3G jukebox (hard disk).   </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"#/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-facelift-activate-mmi-3g-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; import multimedia -&gt; selectionner <strong>[Copy/Ripping] 4/4</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_MMI3g_PLUS_diagnose_settings_importmultimedia-01b4e47b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/import_ripping_mmi3g_vagcoding-af2ca0fd.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-lowering-the-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“52 – Passenger door</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“4</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“2</strong>”:<strong>“Reserve Gear Mirror Dipping active</strong>”<br/>and Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Position Memory for Reserve Gear Mirror Dipping active</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Golf-7-Abaisser-le-retroviseur-passager-lors-de-la-9710a97c.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-microphone-sensitivity-adjustment":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A6 C6 4F facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the intensity of the hands-free system’s microphone.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>For MMI 2G :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“77 – Telephone</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose Channel <strong>131</strong> or <strong>07</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a value expressed in<strong>“dB</strong>” (default value<strong>“0 dB</strong>”) then validate.</p>\n<p><strong>For MMI 3G :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"#/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-facelift-activate-mmi-3g-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>main &gt; diagnostics &gt; settings &gt; Mic sensiblity  </p>\n<p>Choose a value between : -6db/0db/+6db</p>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-mmi-3g-3gp-customized-start-logo":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A6 C6 4F facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To modify and/or customize the home screen logo (Custom Splash Screen) with a personalized image of the MMI 3G and 3GPLUS. <br/><br/>Start by downloading the script file: <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/download/MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen_VAG-Coding.fr.zip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen_VAG-Coding.en.zip</a></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed </strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Then extract the file you just downloaded: MMI 3G 3GP SplashScreen VAG-Coding.en.zip</li>\n<li>Go to the “splashscreens” folder and edit the “startup_generic.png” image if you wish. You can edit this image, modify it or import another image, to have your own startup logo (keep the same PNG format and image size 800×480) or an image found in the “samples” folder (copy it into the “splashscreens” folder with the name startup_generic.png. </li>\n<li>Copy the contents of the MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen folder to a FAT32-formatted SD card (max. 32GB).</li>\n<li>Start your AUDI and let the MMI boot up, it takes a few seconds.</li>\n<li>Disconnect your smartphone’s Bluetooth if there’s a link between it and the MMI, and remove all your SD cards (SD1 &amp; SD2)…</li>\n<li>Then insert the SD card you have prepared into slot SD1.</li>\n<li>You’ll see green text asking you to turn the large knob on your MMI central console, and the message will disappear.</li>\n<li>Wait a few moments. A new message will appear stating that all has gone well and that your image has been imported successfully. </li>\n<li>Restart the MMI using the button combination that corresponds to your AUDI.<br/>Example: Press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right button (3) at the same time.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>If your new start-up screen does not appear when your MMI reboots, go to the green hidden menu<em> (to activate the hidden menu, follow the “Activate MMI 3G or 3GP hidden menu” tutorial).</em></p>\n<p>For <strong>MMI 3GP </strong>: Select in <strong>car </strong>-&gt;<strong> carcodingvehicle </strong>-&gt;<strong> Select n° screen </strong>-&gt;<strong> set cursor to 0</strong>, then restart your MMI.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/splashscreenmmi3gp-6fcb5f6a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>For <strong>MMI 3G</strong>: <strong>car</strong> -&gt; <strong>carcodingvehicle</strong> -&gt; <strong>configuration line</strong> -&gt; <em><strong>[standard] 2/5</strong> (Standard home screen)</em> then restart your MMI.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6876-ad94c126.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Your very own Splash Screen will appear!<br/>Many images are available in the zip file… both the original and modified ones.</p>\n<p><em>A problem?  </em>If the script doesn’t run the first time, try again. You’ve only copied the contents of the MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen folder? Do not copy the folder, just its contents!  <br/>For MMI 3G Basic: If your image does not appear or is truncated, resize the image to 400 by 240.</p>\n<hr/>\n<ul><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A1-cca1d214.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A1-quattro-d5c05d6b.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-ec35ba13.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-allroad-ecfb784b.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-Hybrid-8b3bc272.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6L-da4efe88.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A7-0413e2db.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A8-b82aa2e7.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A8-Hybrid-bf48c947.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Q3-f5806bdd.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Q5-137fb9fc.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RS6-99c35be3.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RS7-973708ca.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RSQ3-82016453.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RSQ5-4b2a2aa7.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S1-8fca826d.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-ff017200.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-png_APR-b51955a9.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-APR-5b67cc13.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S7-1b8e075e.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S8-1a7397d6.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Vierge-e6bcc4e4.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_W12-9cbddbdf.webp\"/></figure></li></ul><a></a><a></a><a></a>","a6-c6-facelift-needle-check":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the scanning of the speedometer needles when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“0</strong>”:<strong>“Gauge Test/Needle Sweep active</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/check_aiguille-9b803756.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-facelift-oil-temperature-boost-via-lap-timer":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a6_4f_facelift-0102d933.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Purpose:</strong> Adds oil temperature and turbo boost to the stopwatch on the ODB screen. (boost only works with petrol engines)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Lap Timer active</strong>”.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/check_aiguille-9b803756.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0782-83aceb84.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-activate-battery-charge-status-in-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates battery charge status in Audi MMI Basic / 2G / 3G.  <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<h2>MMI Basic (Radio Symphony/Concert) :</h2>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 39</strong> </em>then increase the value by <strong>+16</strong></p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>MMI 2G :</h2>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>07 – Control Head</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 01</strong> </em>then adjust the value accordingly:</p>\n<p>x1xxxxxx = show battery status display<br/>x0xxxxxx = do not show battery status display</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 02</strong> (Installation List II (MMI Functionnality) </em>then increase the value by <strong>+32</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the MMI (Press SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button)</em></p>\n<p><em>If the battery does not appear after restarting the MMI, launch the hidden menu (to activate it, see the “activate hidden menu” tutorial, to launch the hidden menu press MENU + CAR (for 6s)).</em></p>\n<p>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; Car Menus Maske -&gt; Battery Level-&gt; Check box</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>MMI 3G :</h2>\n<p><em><strong>WARNING: </strong>You must have activated the Hidden Menu<a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">(Activate MMI 3G hidden menu</a>).</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu press MENU + CAR (for 6s)</em></p>\n<p>car -&gt; carextdevicelist -&gt; battery -&gt; check box</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carmenuoperation -&gt; battery -&gt; select <strong>5</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_MMI3g_PLUS_Hidden_Menue_battery-5a0d0626.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Restart MMI</p>\n<p><em>Press SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g_reset-cdd6298b.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterieMMI2g-b0e8bfbc.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_MMI_3G_PLUS_batterie-69d82b4b.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl-on-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate/deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) on the MMI.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p>4 – Click on “Coding – 07” then “Long Coding Helper”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em><em>Put <strong>2 in </strong>the penultimate digit of the code (0xxxx<strong>?</strong>x).</em></em></p>\n<p>-&gt; 2 = with Daytime Running Lights (selectable via MMI)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a6c6centralelec-1024x630-dac2c92a.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-activate-mmi-2g-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI 2G. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“07 – Display/Control.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 08 </strong></em>(Service Menu) and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Reboot the MMI by pressing SETUP + the Dial + the Upper-Right Button</em></p>\n<p><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (for 6 seconds)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/menu_cache_mmi2g-42dff347.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>","a6-c6-adapting-comfort-functions":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to set comfort functions. Depending on the settings you have made, you can configure comfort closing or comfort opening via the radio remote control or the driver’s door switches.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Code 07</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Set the value to the desired setting:</p>\n<p>+001 = Comfort closure: electric windows by radio remote control  <br/>+002 = Comfort opening: electric windows by radio remote control  <br/>+004 = Comfort closure: sunroof by radio remote control  <br/>+008 = Comfort opening: sunroof via radio remote control<br/>+016 = Comfort closure: power windows via eFH switch on driver’s door  <br/>+032 = Comfort opening: window lift via driver’s door eFH switch  <br/>+064 = Comfort closure: sunroof via driver’s door eFH switch  <br/>+128 = Comfort opening: sunroof via eFH switch on driver’s door  <br/>+256 = comfort closing: window lift via closing button  <br/>+512 = Comfort opening: sunroof via close button</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4L0-910-289_Module46_Coding-c9601d6e.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-automatic-deactivation-of-electric-handbrake-without-seatbelt":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows automatic deactivation of the electric handbrake on start-up without having to fasten the seatbelt.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>53 – Parking Brake</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“25194</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 07</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to<strong> 0</strong></em><br/></p>","a6-c6-automatic-headlight-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_bordnetz_rls_autobahnlicht_regenl-c0c525c9.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-automatic-headlight-activation-in-the-event-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong>, Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_bordnetz_rls_autobahnlicht_regenl-c0c525c9.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-change-mmi-2g-start-logo":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the Splash Screen of the MMI 2G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The hidden menu must be activated</strong> (see: <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-activer-menu-cache-mmi-2g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activating the MMI 2G hidden menu</a> ).</p>\n<p>Launch the Hidden Menu by pressing SETUP + CAR (for 6s)</p>\n<p><br/>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; HU Codierung -&gt; Standby-Bild -&gt; choose value</p>\n<p><em>Coding :</em></p>\n<p>0: Standard MMI 2G screen<br/>1: S6<br/>2: S5<br/>3: RS6<br/>4: RS logo</p>\n<p>Restart the MMI by pressing SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g_reset-cdd6298b.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-change-radio-source-by-pressing-radio":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the radio station by pressing the RADIO button on the MMI 2G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” . 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <strong>Channel</strong><em><strong> </strong></em>(Additional MMI Options)</p>\n<p>Add <strong>4</strong> to your existing code (frequency/source change via active function button)</p>","a6-c6-change-voice-command-language":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the language of the MMI Bluetooth module’s Voice Command.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“77 – Telephone</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Replace the 6th digit of the coding string with the language of your choice:<br/><br/>00x0x00 = Voice Control Off<br/>00x0x10 = German<br/>00x0x20 = English (UK)<br/>00x0x30 = French<br/>00x0x40 = Italian<br/>00x0x50 = Spanish<br/>00x0x60 = Spanish (USA)<br/>00x0x70 = English (USA)<br/>00x0x80 = French (Canada)<br/>00x0x90 = Speaker dependant voice selection</p>","a6-c6-controlled-suspension-calibration":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to recalibrate the pilot-controlled suspension reference height to the original values.  </p>\n<p><strong>Original suspension height</strong> </p>\n<p>Audi A6 (C6) (PR-1BK): 386 mm (front) and 384 mm (rear) <br/>Audi A6 (C6) Allroad (PR-1BY): 388 mm (front) and 380 mm (rear)  </p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites</strong> </p>\n<p>The gear selector must be in neutral (manual gearbox) / in position “P” (automatic gearbox)<br/>Start the engine, it must run throughout the calibration, do not switch off the ignition<br/>All doors must be closed, and not opened during calibration.</p>\n<h3><strong>Measurement of actual suspension height</strong></h3>\n<p>It is necessary to measure and record the actual height of each suspension.<br/>The suspension height is the vertical distance between the middle of the wheel and the lower edge of the fender at the wheel arch.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong> “34 – Correct trim”</strong>. 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31564</strong>”<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”<br/><br/> 5 –<strong> Channel 01</strong>: <em>Left front suspension adjustment </em><br/><em>Enter the previously measured value</em></p>\n<p><strong>Channel 02 </strong>: <em>Front right suspension adjustment </em><br/><em>Enter previously measured value</em></p>\n<p><strong>Channel 03</strong>: <em>Left rear suspension adjustment </em><br/><em>Enter previously measured value</em></p>\n<p><strong>Channel 04</strong>: <em>Right rear suspension adjustment </em><br/><em>Enter previously measured value</em></p>\n<p><strong>Channel 05 </strong>: <em>Set value <strong>1</strong></em></p>","a6-c6-correction-of-odb-consumption-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to correct the fuel consumption display on the on-board computer.  </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible on Mid/High range models</strong>. <br/><em>Note: modifications affect the display of instantaneous consumption, average consumption and fuel quantity.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on <strong>“17 – Instruments”</strong>. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation- 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> <em>“Consumption Correction”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Adjust consumption correction factor between 85% and 115%.</em> <em>(base value: 100)</em></p>\n<p><em>Example 1: Calculation based on volume per distance (e.g. l/100 km): DIS: 9.3 l/100 km. Actual: 9.8 l/100 km. (100, 9,8 / 9,73 ? 105,38) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 105 <br/>Example 2: Calculation based on volume distance (e.g. MPG is: DIS: 23 MPG. Actual: 24 MPG. (100, 23/24 and 95.83) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 96</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/correction-consommation-odb-d51db18e.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-deactivate-activate-electric-handbrake-for-rear-brake-pad-change":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate/activate the electric handbrake in maintenance mode in order to change/replace the rear brake pad/disc linings. (EPB reset / Lining change mode)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/>To start, set the gear lever to P, remove the electric handbrake on the button and preferably connect a battery charger according to the vehicle manual. Check that there are no faults/errors before starting basic setup.<br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“53 – Parking Brake</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Basic setting</strong> <strong>– 04</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel <strong>007</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Click on<strong>“Go</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Basic Settings: <strong>OFF</strong> during the procedure, then <strong>ON</strong> when finished (yellow arrow).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/53epb007-8e9a2db6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>A fault message will appear on your ODB indicating<strong>“Parking brake fault</strong>” and an LED in the parking brake switch, but this is normal and should be ignored.<br/><br/> 7 – Once finished, go back (Done, Go Back) until the program closes.<br/><br/> 8 – Switch off the vehicle’s ignition, then disconnect the VAG-COM cable<br/><br/> 9 – <strong>Change the linings on both sides!</strong><br/><br/><br/></p>\n<p><strong>To reactivate the electric handbrake :</strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>10</strong> – With engine off and ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>11</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>12</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“53 – Parking Brake</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>13</strong> – Click on<strong>“Basic setting – 04</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>14</strong> – Select Channel <strong>006</strong><br/><br/><strong>15</strong> – Click on<strong>“Go</strong>”.<br/><br/>Basic Settings: <strong>OFF</strong> during the procedure, then <strong>ON </strong>when finished (yellow arrow).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/53epb006-52154901.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>16</strong> – Once finished, go back (Done, Go Back) until the program is closed.</p>\n<p><strong>17</strong> – Switch off the ignition and disconnect the VAG-COM cable.</p>","a6-c6-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Put <strong>0</strong> in the penultimate digit of the coding (xxxxx<strong>?</strong>x).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-disable-rear-wiper-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear windshield wiper during reversing when the front windshield wipers are operating.  </p>\n<p><em><strong>For A6 C6 Avant and Allroad only.  </strong></em><br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“12151</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 16</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p><em>Set value to </em><strong>“0”</strong> to deactivate and <strong>“1”</strong> to activate  </p>","a6-c6-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“46- Central Conv.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong> “Adaptation – 10”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 50</strong> (Adaptive Brake Light in the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Add the following values: </em><br/><em>+1: Activate brake light flashing</em><br/><em>+2: Increase braking zone (sedans only)<br/></em></p>","a6-c6-led-tail-lights-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the activation of LED taillights after replacing the halogen taillights with pre-facelift LEDs (retrofit).</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add<strong> +131072</strong> to existing coding </em> (Highline / LED light)</p>","a6-c6-lock-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-mmi-2g":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the CD/DVD eject button on the MMI 2G.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 68</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(Eject Button inactive (Anti-Theft))</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the MMI 2G.</em></p>\n<p>To eject the CD/DVD, set the value to <strong>0</strong> for normal use of the button.  </p>","a6-c6-lock-unlock-confirmation-beeps":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Used to set confirmation of door locking/unlocking with beep (alarm).  </p>\n<p><strong>The vehicle must be equipped with the factory-installed alarm</strong>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>+2048</strong> to existing coding.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4L0-910-289_Module46_Coding-c9601d6e.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-lower-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically. (For A6 phase 1)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“52 – Passenger door</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Add <strong>+128</strong> to the original coding<br/>Example: the original code is 0002682… The new code is 0002810</p>","a6-c6-mmi-2g-speed-alert-and-odb-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the display of the speed alert setting and on-board computer activation on the MMI 2G screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The hidden menu must be activated</strong> (see: <a href=\"#/audi/a6-c6/a6-c6-activate-mmi-2g-hidden-menu\">Activating the MMI 2G hidden menu</a> ).</p>\n<p>Launch the Hidden Menu by pressing SETUP + CAR (for 6s)</p>\n<p>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; APK 0x01, 0x0B, 0x0C -&gt; Bordcomputer -&gt; Check box</p>\n<p>Scroll to the bottom of the menu<br/>Select “Accept changes”.</p>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Press SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g_reset-cdd6298b.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-parking-aid-display-on-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the radar display on the MMI with the Audi Parking System rear option only.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“76 – Parking Assist.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Replace the second “0” (from the left) with a “2”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Ex: Replace “<strong>0001216</strong>” with “<strong>0201216</strong>”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Coding :</em><br/><em>0?xxxxx: Visual Display</em><br/><em>0 = without Visual Display on MMI</em><br/><em>2 = with Visual Display on MMI</em></p>\n<p><strong>Module Compatibility List</strong></p>\n<figure><table><tbody><tr><td>4F0 910 283</td><td>4 sensors (no graphic support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 A</td><td>4 sensors (no graphic support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 B</td><td>4 sensors (graphic support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 C</td><td>8 sensors (graphic support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 D</td><td>4 sensors (graphic support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 E</td><td>8 sensors (graphic support, rear view camera support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 F</td><td>4 sensors (graphic support, rear view camera support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 G</td><td>8 sensors (graphic support, rear view camera support)</td></tr><tr><td>4F0 910 283 H</td><td>8 sensors (graphic support, rear view camera support)</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>","a6-c6-rear-lights-activated-with-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rear lights to turn on when the daytime running lights (Scandinavian DRL) are activated. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Replace the last digit of the coding string with ” <strong>2</strong> “<br/>Example: 0xxxxx2</p>","a6-c6-remove-electric-handbrake-without-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows the driver to release the electric parking brake without fastening their seat belt and without having their foot on the brake.  </p>\n<p><strong>This can be dangerous if you have children or pets in the vehicle</strong>.  </p>\n<p><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>53 – Parking Brake</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“25194</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to<strong> 0</strong></em><br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/pf2-f86aa92b.webp\"/></figure>","a6-c6-reprogramming-a-new-battery":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to reprogram / recode the new battery of all its data after replacement.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! Depending on your calculator, select 61 or 19</strong> <strong>(CAN or UDS)</strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<h2>61-Batterie Regul. CAN </h2>\n<p>This procedure concerns the replacement of the battery in vehicles using a separate battery management control module.<br/>Address 61: Regul Battery. Labels: 4F0-910-181.lbl Reference SW: 4F0 910 181 E HW: 4F0 915 181 A Component: ENERGIEMANAGER H12 0490 Subsystem 1 – Part No: 000 915 105 C Component: von VA0 2502160103 Coding: 303030393135313035432056413032353032313630313033 Shop N °: WSC 54332 321 22222 </p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“61 – Battery Regul. </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose the <strong>battery (slave) classified n°1</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In<strong>“Coding battery</strong>” :  </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enter the new Battery Part number (10 or 11 digits).</li>\n<li>Enter the new battery serial number (10 digits).</li>\n<li>Select the new battery supplier.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>[OK]<br/>[! Do – it]<br/>[Close Controller, Go Back – 06]</p>\n<p>Your new battery should now be coded, and the battery control module should be aware of the new battery.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>19-CAN Gateway using CAN</h2>\n<p>This procedure concerns battery replacement in vehicles using a battery management control module which is a slave / subsystem of the CAN gateway.Address 19: CAN Gateway (J533) Labels: 8T0-907-468.clb Reference SW: 8T0 907 468 Q HW: 8T0 907 468 L Component: GW-EBM 5CAN-M H10 0095 Subsystem 1 – Part No SW: 8K0 915 181 B HW: 8K0 915 181 B Component: J367-BDM H04 0150</p>\n<p>Installation of a new battery requires use of the [Long Adaptation-0A function] under the 19-CAN-Gateway control module. . Follow the on-screen instructions to enter the part number, supplier, serial number and any long new value.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“19 – <strong>Gateway </strong>CAN</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Long Adaptation-0A</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select <strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p>VCED will populate instructions in the form of a pop-up balloon with formatting. For example:Format: nnnnnnnnnnn XXX zzzzzzzzzz N = battery part number (11 digits) X = battery supplier (3 digits) Z = battery serial number (10 digits) </p>\n<p>[Add to log] Saving the original value in a log is strongly recommended.<br/>Enter the New Battery details in the new field value.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note, the new value must be 26 (alpha numeric) characters in total, including spaces! If in doubt, check the logbook for the original battery formatting details. </li>\n</ul>\n<p>[Test]<br/>[Save]<br/>The value has been accepted by the controller the new battery coding is complete<br/>[Done, Back]<br/>[Close Controller, Go Back – 06]</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>19-CAN Gateway help (UDS / ODX)</h2>\n<p>This procedure concerns battery replacement in vehicles using a battery management control module which is a slave / subsystem of the CAN gateway.Address 19: CAN Gateway (J533) Labels: None Reference SW: 4G0 907 468 E HW: 4G0 907 468 A Component: J533 – Gateway H08 0213 ASAM Dataset: EV_GatewUDS 001025 Battery Monitoring Control Module: Subsystem 1 – Part No SW: 8×0 915 181 HW: 8×0 915 181 Component: J367-BDM H07 0140</p>\n<p>Installing a new battery requires the use of the [Adaptation-10 function] under the 19-CAN-Gateway control module. Use the drop-down menus to enter the part number, vendor, and serial number information located on the new battery. </p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Adaptation batterie-Capacité nominal de la batterie</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but towards the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a nominal value indicated on your battery, e.g.<strong>“70Ah</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Adaptation batterie-Fabriquant de batterie</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the corresponding brand:<br/>Ex: In the case of the VARTA E39, choose<strong>“VAO</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Adaptation batterie-Numéro de série de la batterie</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, enter the corresponding serial number:<br/>Warning, insert only the <strong>last 10 digits</strong> of the serial number.</p>\n<p>The value has been accepted by the controller the new battery coding is complete<br/>[Done, Back]<br/>[Close Controller, Go Back – 06]</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Battery</strong></p>\n<p>The vehicle’s battery is housed in the engine compartment and protected by a battery tray. Battery size and design depend on engine version, equipment and national variant. Standard, EFB and AGM batteries are used.<br/>Vehicles with petrol engines and start/stop systems are fitted with EFB batteries, while vehicles with diesel engines and start/stop systems are fitted with AGM batteries.   Vehicles with stationary chauﬀage generally have an AGM battery.</p>\n<p><strong>EFB</strong></p>\n<p>An EFB (Enhanced Flooded Battery) is a reinforced wet battery. The positive plate inside the battery is coated with an additional polyester canvas. This gives the battery’s active mass additional support on the plate. The alternating cycle resistance of these batteries is superior to that of standard batteries. During charging, the EFB battery is treated like a standard battery.</p>\n<p><strong>AGM battery</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-agm-f4b81a74.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In AGM batteries (short for Absorbent Glass Mat), the battery’s electrolyte is retained in a micro-porous glass mat. An AGM battery is not only even more resistant to alternating cycles than an EFB battery, but also watertight. When charging, follow the charger’s operating instructions and select the AGM battery program if necessary.</p>\n<p>In the case of AGM batteries, the automotive battery electrolyte is retained in a micro-porous glass mat. In addition to<br/>increased resistance to alternating cycles, an AGM battery is characterized by its good sealing properties. Waterproofing is of crucial importance<br/>, especially when the battery is installed in<br/>the passenger compartment. When charging, please follow the charger’s operating instructions and select the program for<br/>AGM battery, if applicable.</p>\n<p>Below we see the battery brand, serial number and manufacturer.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-124711ff.webp\"/></figure>"};
